# The second of `scan_encapsed_part_string`'s two live parameters:
# `is_execution_string`, which is the difference between `"…"` and `` `…` ``.
#
# php's scanner serves both with one function and tells them apart only by
# which terminal the parse state asked for, so this file is the control on
# `double-quoted-string.php` rather than a copy of it: a seating that answered
# only the double-quoted member would leave this one blind, and a walk that
# hardcoded `"` as the close would run this backtick body to end of input and
# refuse.
#
# The interpolation is here for a reason too. `$d` ends the content run and
# resumes it, so the file exercises the boundary in the middle of a body and
# not just at its ends: `ls ` is [12, 15) and the variable [15, 17).
#
# Claims are tree-sitter's tree over these bytes.
roots 1
mends 0
holds shell_command_expression
holds variable_name
lacks text
spans shell_command_expression 11 18
spans string_content 12 15
